# Probes use the real client path and return a script-friendly status.

```console
$ OPENROUTER_API_KEY=trycmd-probe-basic lllm --catalog catalog.toml probe --model openrouter/fixture
passed openrouter/fixture · 7 input · 2 output · [..]

$ LLLM_MODEL=openrouter/fixture OPENROUTER_API_KEY=trycmd-probe-json lllm --catalog catalog.toml probe --reasoning-effort low --timeout 2s --json
{
  "version": 1,
  "route": "openrouter/fixture",
  "outcome": {
    "status": "passed"
  },
  "latency_ms": [..],
  "usage": {
    "input": 11,
    "output": 3,
    "reasoning": 0,
    "cache_read": 0,
    "cache_write": 0
  }
}

$ OPENROUTER_API_KEY=trycmd-probe-tools lllm --catalog catalog.toml probe --model-query fixture --tools
passed openrouter/fixture · 60 input · 6 output · [..]

$ OPENROUTER_API_KEY=trycmd-probe-incorrect lllm --catalog catalog.toml probe -m openrouter/fixture --tools
? 1
incorrect openrouter/fixture · the model answered without calling the tool · 9 input · 1 output · [..]

$ OPENROUTER_API_KEY=trycmd-probe-failure lllm --catalog catalog.toml probe -m openrouter/fixture
? 1
failed openrouter/fixture · authentication · provider openrouter probe key rejected · status=401 · code=invalid_api_key · 0 input · 0 output · [..]

$ OPENROUTER_API_KEY=trycmd-probe-timeout lllm --catalog catalog.toml probe -m openrouter/fixture --timeout 5ms
? 1
failed openrouter/fixture · timeout · [..] · 0 input · 0 output · [..]

$ lllm --catalog catalog.toml probe -m missing/not-real
? 1
failed missing/not-real · model_selection · provider `missing` was not found · 0 input · 0 output · [..]

```
